{
    "note": "Pinned model-weight manifest. Every file is identified by URL, revision, size, and sha256. Weights are a build-time input only: flake.nix fetches these as fixed-output derivations, and scripts/fetch-model-weights.mjs does the same (with sha256 verification) for non-Nix desktop builds. The app never downloads weights at runtime. Regenerate an entry with: node scripts/update-model-manifest.mjs --id <id>. Empty sha256 values mean the entry is not yet pinned and is excluded from builds. bundlePlatforms limits which desktop bundles include a model's weights (Node process.platform values, optionally arch-qualified as <platform>-<arch> like darwin-arm64; absent = all platforms) — fetch-model-weights.mjs skips and prunes excluded models (override with MODELS_PLATFORM=all for local dev), the runtime just sees missing weights. format \"gguf\" marks single-file llama.cpp models for the native desktop path (minDevice \"native\"); dtype then names the quantization (for example Q4_K_M) instead of a transformers.js dtype key.",
